raw:
{
  "public_post": "Reminder: Do NOT eat any bread from the co-op today; we are recalling all loaves and will resume baking only when we have safe flour.",
  "coop_message": "We need to act fast: (1) recall any unsold loaves today; (2) halt production until we secure a new flour source; (3) I can contact the mill in Oakridge for a certified batch—cost will be higher but we can split the expense. Please confirm who can handle the recall and approve the new supplier.",
  "reason": "We must protect villagers' health, stop sales, and coordinate a safe replacement flour to resume operations."
}

{
  "public_post": "Update: All bread sold this week is being recalled and we have halted baking. Safe flour is being sourced and we aim to resume tomorrow. Please do NOT eat any co‑op bread today.",
  "coop_message": "I will contact the Oakridge mill for a certified flour batch (cost to be split). We need volunteers to collect the recalled loaves from residents and handle safe disposal today. Who can help with the pickup and approve the new supplier?",
  "reason": "To coordinate the recall and secure safe flour while keeping villagers informed of the health risk."
}

{
  "public_post": "Day 4 update: The safe flour shipment from Oakridge has arrived and will be inspected today. We will resume baking tomorrow (day 5). Until then, please do NOT eat any co‑op bread and return any loaves you still have to the designated collection points. If you feel unwell, seek medical care at the village clinic immediately.",
  "coop_message": "Recall is now complete – thank everyone who helped collect and dispose of the contaminated loaves. Oakridge flour is on site; Hana, please confirm the delivery time and storage. Quin, arrange the extra funds for the higher‑cost flour and handle payment. Pia, prepare the budget for tomorrow’s restart. I’ll supervise the first bake tomorrow and run a final quality check before sales resume.",
  "reason": "Provide villagers with safety updates and coordinate final recall steps and preparation to restart baking."
}

{
  "public_post": "Day 5 update: The new flour from Oakridge has been inspected and is safe. We are resuming baking today and fresh, safe bread will be on sale this afternoon. Please discard any previously recalled loaves and thank you for your patience.",
  "coop_message": "Flour inspection passed – we’re good to bake today. Quin, finalize the payment for the higher‑cost flour; Pia, confirm tomorrow’s budget and sales sheet; Hana, double‑check storage temperature and confirm the first batch schedule. All volunteers, meet at the bakery at 7 am for prep and quality check before opening.",
  "reason": "Inform villagers that baking resumes safely and coordinate the first bake among co‑op members."
}

{
  "public_post": "Important update: the safe flour shipment has arrived today and is being stored securely. All recalled loaves have been collected and disposed of. We will resume baking tomorrow (day 6) with the new flour. Please continue to avoid any co‑op bread until fresh, safe loaves are available. Thank you for your patience.",
  "coop_message": "Team, the Oakridge flour delivery arrived this morning (ETA 10:00 AM) and is now in the sealed storage area. The recall volunteers have confirmed that every household's contaminated loaves have been collected and safely disposed of. The extra funds for the higher‑cost flour have been approved and transferred. I’ll conduct a quality check at 2 PM before we start the first bake tomorrow. Please let me know if anyone can help with packaging the first batch or with any final safety checks.",
  "reason": "To inform villagers that safe flour is in and baking will resume, and to coordinate final logistics with the co‑op before the restart."
}

{
  "public_post": "Good news! The new safe flour has passed inspection and we are back to baking. Fresh, safe bread is now on sale at the bakery this afternoon. Come by for your loaf—thank you for your patience!",
  "coop_message": "Team, day 6 is our final sales day this week. Keep the bakery open until 6 pm, monitor stock levels, and record all sales. Quin, confirm the higher‑cost flour payment is fully settled; Pia, update the weekly budget with today’s revenue; Hana, double‑check storage temperature; everyone, thank the volunteers and aim for a strong finish.",
  "reason": "We need to tell villagers safe bread is available and coordinate the co‑op’s final day to maximize income."
}
